    narr:narration """The discourse surrounding the [signed-manifest deployment gate](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_1) centers on the tension between institutional conservation and operational agility. As of July 2026, the narrative is dominated by a [technical and formal insistence](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_3) on the legitimacy of the manifest as a non-negotiable precondition. This [procedural framing](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_5) emphasizes the gate as a concrete, present-tense requirement for system integrity. However, the trajectory is not monolithic; it includes [historical reflections](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_2) that contrast past rationales with current requirements, introducing a layer of skepticism regarding whether these gates function as genuine security measures or merely as authority-ranking mechanisms. The discussion remains open on whether the manifest requirement will tighten into a more rigid automated enforcement or if it faces erosion through bypasses necessitated by shifting operational demands.""" ;
